<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wadai Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wadai, Wadai Sultanate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wadai Empire was a Muslim sultanate in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>, in what is now eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>, founded around 1611 when Abd al-Karim overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunjur">Tunjur</a> rulers. Its capital was initially at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wara">Wara</a>. Wadai grew powerful through the trans-Saharan trade, especially the route north to Benghazi, and through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slave-raiding">slave raiding</a>, and it remained independent until French conquest in the early twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wadai-empire.jpg" alt="Wadai Empire" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gabagool · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CentralEastAfrica1750.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
